        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "RFC: Claws",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds a draft RFC for Capability Packs: versioned package-set manifests that resolve through hosted feeds and existing OpenClaw install policy.\n\n## Motivation\n\nOpenClaw has packages, skills, plugins, compatible bundles, and hosted feeds, but not a focused way to describe a governed scenario-level set of capabilities to inspect, plan, install, and later update together.\n\n## Notes\n\n- References RFC 0009 as the feed dependency.\n- Keeps packs distinct from packages, plugin bundles, and Agent Pack/workspace-template proposals.\n- Includes a staged PR stack: terminology, schema/parser, read-only planning, feed entry integration, install policy integration, install, provenance/status, update semantics, and publishing.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `git diff --check`\n",
